{"texts":[{"text":"Architecture shaped by place, culture, and continuity rather than formal invention alone. Mix of tradition and modernity","bbox":{"x":145,"y":790,"w":793,"h":70},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"16.8px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start"},{"text":"Where function alone was never enough. These architects pushed form, material, and structure into territory that was con","bbox":{"x":148,"y":669,"w":788,"h":69},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"16.8px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start"},{"text":"Architecture at the scale of civilization — civic, institutional, and built to outlast the moment. These buildings draw ","bbox":{"x":147,"y":729,"w":790,"h":52},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"16.8px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start"},{"text":"The movement that broke from European convention before Europe finished writing its manifesto. Buildings designed around","bbox":{"x":150,"y":608,"w":787,"h":52},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"16.8px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start"},{"text":"Contextual & Transitional Architecture","bbox":{"x":1022,"y":728,"w":284,"h":62},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"60px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start"},{"text":"Organic & Early Modernism","bbox":{"x":1115,"y":546,"w":185,"h":62},"fontFamily":"\"IBM Plex Mono\", sans-serif","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"400","letterSpacing":"normal","lineHeight":"60px","textTransform":"none","color":"#ffffff","textAlign":"start